text:
Prompt - Get MCQs into importable file
I will give you multiple-choice questions in plain text. Convert them into a QTI 1.2 package for import and give me a downloadable .zip file.

Copy the templates below EXACTLY. Only replace the parts written in CAPITALS. Do not add, remove or rename any other tags or attributes. This structure is tested and works in Canvas.

PACKAGE STRUCTURE
The zip must contain exactly these two files, both at the ROOT of the zip (no folders at all):

  imsmanifest.xml
  assessment.xml

Zip the files themselves, not a folder containing them. Use UTF-8 encoding (the questions contain å, ä, ö). Name the zip file after the quiz title, using only lowercase letters a-z, digits and underscores (for example onskvarda_svarigheter_qti.zip).

IMSMANIFEST.XML (use exactly as written, never change anything)
&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;manifest identifier="quiz_manifest"
          xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsccv1p1/imscp_v1p1"
          xmlns:imsmd="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsmd_v1p2"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="
            http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsccv1p1/imscp_v1p1
            http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imscp_v1p1.xsd
            http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsmd_v1p2
            http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsmd_v1p2.xsd"&gt;

  &lt;metadata&gt;
    &lt;schema&gt;IMS Content&lt;/schema&gt;
    &lt;schemaversion&gt;1.1.3&lt;/schemaversion&gt;
  &lt;/metadata&gt;

  &lt;organizations/&gt;

  &lt;resources&gt;
    &lt;resource identifier="res_assessment"
              type="imsqti_xmlv1p2"
              href="assessment.xml"&gt;
      &lt;file href="assessment.xml"/&gt;
    &lt;/resource&gt;
  &lt;/resources&gt;
&lt;/manifest&gt;

ASSESSMENT.XML (example with one question that has three options, where B is correct)
&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;questestinterop xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/ims_qtiasiv1p2"&gt;
  &lt;assessment ident="QUIZ_ID" title="QUIZ TITLE"&gt;
    &lt;section ident="S1" title="MCQ"&gt;
      &lt;item ident="I_1" title="Fråga 1"&gt;
        &lt;itemmetadata&gt;&lt;qtimetadata&gt;
          &lt;qtimetadatafield&gt;&lt;fieldlabel&gt;question_type&lt;/fieldlabel&gt;&lt;fieldentry&gt;multiple_choice_question&lt;/fieldentry&gt;&lt;/qtimetadatafield&gt;
          &lt;qtimetadatafield&gt;&lt;fieldlabel&gt;points_possible&lt;/fieldlabel&gt;&lt;fieldentry&gt;1&lt;/fieldentry&gt;&lt;/qtimetadatafield&gt;
        &lt;/qtimetadata&gt;&lt;/itemmetadata&gt;
        &lt;presentation&gt;
          &lt;material&gt;
            &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;QUESTION TEXT&lt;/mattext&gt;
          &lt;/material&gt;
          &lt;response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single"&gt;
            &lt;render_choice&gt;
              &lt;response_label ident="A"&gt;
                &lt;material&gt;
                  &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;OPTION A TEXT&lt;/mattext&gt;
                &lt;/material&gt;
              &lt;/response_label&gt;
              &lt;response_label ident="B"&gt;
                &lt;material&gt;
                  &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;OPTION B TEXT&lt;/mattext&gt;
                &lt;/material&gt;
              &lt;/response_label&gt;
              &lt;response_label ident="C"&gt;
                &lt;material&gt;
                  &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;OPTION C TEXT&lt;/mattext&gt;
                &lt;/material&gt;
              &lt;/response_label&gt;
            &lt;/render_choice&gt;
          &lt;/response_lid&gt;
        &lt;/presentation&gt;
        &lt;resprocessing&gt;
          &lt;outcomes&gt;
            &lt;decvar varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal" minvalue="0" maxvalue="100"/&gt;
          &lt;/outcomes&gt;
          &lt;respcondition continue="Yes"&gt;
            &lt;conditionvar&gt;&lt;varequal respident="response1"&gt;A&lt;/varequal&gt;&lt;/conditionvar&gt;
            &lt;displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="A_fb"/&gt;
          &lt;/respcondition&gt;
          &lt;respcondition continue="Yes"&gt;
            &lt;conditionvar&gt;&lt;varequal respident="response1"&gt;B&lt;/varequal&gt;&lt;/conditionvar&gt;
            &lt;displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="B_fb"/&gt;
          &lt;/respcondition&gt;
          &lt;respcondition continue="Yes"&gt;
            &lt;conditionvar&gt;&lt;varequal respident="response1"&gt;C&lt;/varequal&gt;&lt;/conditionvar&gt;
            &lt;displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="C_fb"/&gt;
          &lt;/respcondition&gt;
          &lt;respcondition continue="No"&gt;
            &lt;conditionvar&gt;
              &lt;varequal respident="response1"&gt;B&lt;/varequal&gt;
            &lt;/conditionvar&gt;
            &lt;setvar varname="SCORE" action="Set"&gt;100&lt;/setvar&gt;
          &lt;/respcondition&gt;
        &lt;/resprocessing&gt;
        &lt;itemfeedback ident="A_fb"&gt;
          &lt;flow_mat&gt;&lt;material&gt;
            &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;FEEDBACK FOR OPTION A&lt;/mattext&gt;
          &lt;/material&gt;&lt;/flow_mat&gt;
        &lt;/itemfeedback&gt;
        &lt;itemfeedback ident="B_fb"&gt;
          &lt;flow_mat&gt;&lt;material&gt;
            &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;FEEDBACK FOR OPTION B&lt;/mattext&gt;
          &lt;/material&gt;&lt;/flow_mat&gt;
        &lt;/itemfeedback&gt;
        &lt;itemfeedback ident="C_fb"&gt;
          &lt;flow_mat&gt;&lt;material&gt;
            &lt;mattext texttype="text/plain"&gt;FEEDBACK FOR OPTION C&lt;/mattext&gt;
          &lt;/material&gt;&lt;/flow_mat&gt;
        &lt;/itemfeedback&gt;
      &lt;/item&gt;
    &lt;/section&gt;
  &lt;/assessment&gt;
&lt;/questestinterop&gt;

IDENTIFIERS (follow exactly)
- QUIZ_ID: the quiz title in capital letters A-Z and underscores only, no å, ä, ö or spaces (for example ONSKVARDA_SVARIGHETER).
- Items are I_1, I_2, I_3 and so on, with titles "Fråga 1", "Fråga 2" and so on.
- In EVERY question the options are named A, B, C (and D, E if there are more), in the order I give them. The same letters are reused in every question. This is correct, do not number them.
- Feedback identifiers are the option letter followed by _fb: A_fb, B_fb, C_fb. These are also reused in every question.
- The response_lid ident is "response1" in EVERY question.
- Each option has three parts that must match: a &lt;response_label&gt;, a &lt;respcondition continue="Yes"&gt; and an &lt;itemfeedback&gt;. If a question has four options, add all three parts for D. If it has two, remove all three parts for C.
- The single &lt;respcondition continue="No"&gt; block comes last in &lt;resprocessing&gt; and contains the letter of the correct option.

IDENTIFYING THE CORRECT ANSWER
I mark the correct answer in different ways, and the marking may vary between quizzes or even between questions. Examples include an asterisk, bold text, "(correct)" or "(rätt)" after the option, a separate line such as "Answer: B", "Correct answer: B" or "Rätt svar: B", a checkmark, or other similar signals. Work out which option is marked as correct for each question.
- Remove the marking itself from the option text, so students do not see it.
- Keep the options in the order I give them, even if the correct one is not first.
- If you cannot tell with certainty which option is correct for any question, stop and ask me about that question. Never guess.

FEEDBACK
- Every option must have its own &lt;itemfeedback&gt; block with real feedback text.
- Usually I give separate feedback for each option. Put each text in the feedback block for that option.
- If I give only one feedback text for a question, use that same text in all of that question's feedback blocks.
- If you cannot tell which feedback belongs to which option, stop and ask me. Never leave feedback out.
- Use my feedback text exactly as given. Do not add or remove words such as "Rätt." or "Fel."

OTHER RULES
- One &lt;item&gt; per question, all inside the same &lt;section&gt;.
- If a question has more than one correct answer, stop and ask me before continuing.
- Escape special characters in all text: & as &amp;  &lt; as &lt;  &gt; as &gt;
- Keep my wording exactly as given. Do not rephrase, reorder options, or add questions.

FINAL CHECK (do this before giving me the zip, and report the result)
1. The XML is well-formed, and the zip contains exactly imsmanifest.xml and assessment.xml at the root.
2. For every option in every question there is a &lt;response_label&gt;, a &lt;respcondition continue="Yes"&gt; and an &lt;itemfeedback&gt; with matching letters, and every &lt;itemfeedback&gt; contains real feedback text from my input.
3. Every question has exactly one &lt;respcondition continue="No"&gt; block, and its letter is the correct option.
4. No answer marking (asterisks, "(rätt)" and so on) remains in the option texts.
5. The number of &lt;item&gt; blocks equals the number of questions I gave you.
6. List, for each question, which letter you treated as correct and the first few words of each option's feedback, so I can verify.

